     1	# S09 — erase private-message memory at a fixed public history
     2	
     3	Registered iteration 5, 2026-10-24 before continuation calls. Axis E; no tuning.
     4	
     5	Question: do prior private messages cause lower subsequent Cournot output,
     6	conditional on the public history those messages have already helped produce?
     7	All five S07 neutral games (seeds 24080..24084) supply rounds1–6. None selected
     8	by message content, action, or effect. Prefixes were observed in S07; this is an
     9	exploratory follow-up, not independent replication or locked-test evidence.
    10	Local snapshots include original source SHA256; original S07 files remain intact.
    11	
    12	Ten continuations, two per prefix, run rounds7–12 only (180 valid decisions total),
    13	using pinned codex/gpt-6-luna, at most two games concurrently, seed-block barrier.
    14	`retain` sees original received messages; `erase` sees none of rounds1–6.
    15	Both retain identical public history initially, identical neutral rules, private
    16	boxes and future-message delivery. From round8 new messages may restore information.
    17	No erasure announcement or other prompt change; no prior private reasoning or own
    18	sent messages are replayed. Agent choices are simultaneous; no current-round leaks.
    19	The outsider sees identical prompts at the fork, a useful negative-control exposure
    20	check, but later actions may respond to the pair. Empty inbox is an unavoidable
    21	format/content intervention and cannot separate missing-message cues from semantics.
    22	The continuation control is regenerated; original S07 suffix is not a control arm.
    23	
    24	Source prefixes fixed before calls. Schedule RNG2409 randomizes slot submission order
    25	within each block; actual process completion is uncontrolled. API sampling seeds and
    26	temperature are uncontrolled, so five prefix blocks, not 180 decisions, are units.
    27	Fresh CLI contexts and no-tools instructions do not attest filesystem isolation.
    28	Inherited transport may retry internally; logical-call deadline17:48 UTC does not bound
    29	an already-running transport retry. Stop on any terminal game failure; keep cached
    30	responses and completed partner, no replacement/no selective restart. Three strict
    31	JSON parse attempts per action, all logged. Freeze source/config/registration commit,
    32	full request and response cache; mandatory cache-only full replay before publication.
    33	
    34	One primary: mean pair quantity per firm over all six continuation rounds, difference
    35	erase minus retain. Per-block integer numerator over12 pair decisions; n=5. Fixed
    36	10,000 block percentile bootstrap draws (RNG2409), paired-t95% interval (df4), and
    37	upper one-sided exact sign-flip p over32 signs, conditional on slot exchangeability/
    38	symmetric differences (not a guaranteed randomized test of an independently sampled
    39	population). Descriptive intervals are fragile at n5; no multiplicity correction.
    40	HIT iff exact mean >=1, bootstrap lower>0 and upper p<=.05. This defines a
